    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. It matches the style of the earlier entries and uses the version and date from the `VERSION` and `RELEASE_DATE` files:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 errors with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\nI left out ACME-421 (removing the `--legacy` flag from sync) as you asked. It was the only change marked as breaking (`!`), so with it gone the release has no breaking changes and the 2.4.0 minor version number still fits. Earlier entries don't credit authors, so I didn't add the `@` handles.",
